const SEARCH_INDEX = [{"t": "Arcy Ivory", "u": "characters/arcy-ivory.html", "y": "character", "g": "\"The ends will justify the means.\"", "a": "anti-villain assassin's guild", "f": "Ane Grimm a78bdb She/Her or They/Them Human 22 Farmer/Assassin 1233 Ivory Farm Assassin's Guild Ivory family Arcy", "b": "Was a farmer, now working a double life as a new Assassin's guild member. Father got sick and mother died, so she has to take care of the family mainly on her own. Working as assassin for the money, to take care of her family and get medical care for her father. Goes under the assassin name of Grimm. Slightly past shoulder length, wolf cut, blond with streaks of dark blue dyed hair, with my eyes being a light violet purple. Short, 5'5. Average build, slightly on the lankier side. Brash, bold, uncaring of many other people's opinions. Sometimes tries to appear tough and uncaring from the outside, but secretly soft and nice. Clingy and a little possessive to close friends. Somewhat slow and not super smart, very clumsy and air headed. Very independent, doesn't like to be chained down. Always wanted/wants to go on grand adventures, but never got a chance to for a long time. Will do anything to keep her little siblings and family safe. Born into a farming family on the outskirts of the kingdom, Arcy Ivory always wanted to be more than just her family legacy. However, she's chained down by her father's sudden illness, needing to help out and farm all day to provide for her 2 little sisters and 1 little brother. When she finally gets the opportunity to go out into the world, she takes it. Arcy accidentally gets caught up in a assassination attempt when royals are visiting the town. She has to run with the real assassins, at first distrusting of them. When they see that she can fight, they try to enlist her to join them, the Assassins Guild. She initially refuses, but ends up joining when seeing how much money they could offer her and her family, going by Grimm as her code name. She now works as a farmer by day, assassin by night. Person Relation Notes --- --- --- ● Cherri Ivory Younger Sister Protects fiercly Knows how to use scythe and farming tools Taught hand-to-hand combat by Assassins Guild Taught stealth by Assassins Guild Sub arc 1 villain. Protagonist of side story. Her backstory, the Vellhaven attempt, and how she ends up in the Guild, assassination attempt on Silver - [ ]"}, {"t": "Cherri Ivory", "u": "characters/cherri-ivory.html", "y": "character", "g": "Youngest sister of the Ivory family", "a": "child", "f": "she/her human 9 None 1246 Ivory Farm Ivory family Arcy", "b": "Arcy's youngest sister and the youngest of all 4 siblings. Didn't know their mother. Enjoys nature, but is physically weak so she gets sick often. Likes taking care of hurt weaker animals. Follows Arcy around and interferes with her double life. Long golden-blond hair, and a short, stubby body. Quite sensitive and weak physically, with pale, light skin. Tends to get sick quite often due to this fact. Wide, curious eyes. Loves to explore and go out into the farm field and woods, but often gets lost or sick while she's out there. Trusts Arcy with everything and likes to follow her around, which interferes with Arcy's double life. Is a full on pacifist, and likes taking care of small, weaker animals and such. Restricted to her home and her bed quite often because of illness, which she gets sad about sometimes, though she gets over it quite fast typically. The last born of Arcy's family before her mother passed, she's the youngest child. Just nine years old, she's doted on and cared for by all of Vellhaven when she goes out, which she does whenever she gets the chance. She didn't know her mother that well, like her siblings did, which makes her sad and wants to learn more about her. Person Relation Notes --- --- --- ● Arcy Ivory Older Sister Fast, small, can run around quickly. Knows the forest well. People person, gets along with people easily Arcy's younger sister, interferes with her double life. - [ ]"}, {"t": "Lorian Eros", "u": "characters/lorian-eros.html", "y": "character", "g": "3rd Royal Prince of the kingdom", "a": "royalty MC love interest", "f": "3rd Prince Dummy Prince the third He/Him Human 20 3rd Prince 1235 Amphora Royal Family Eros Family Arcy", "b": "The third royal prince. The brashest and most outgoing prince, he enjoys swordsmanship and the outside world/nature, A love interest for Silver, he was the first to drag her to the capital when she saved him from a chimera in the forest. Tall, brown haired, distinguished looking. Messy short brown hair, with young, energetic eyes. Wears very adventurer-eques outfits, though more fancy and royal. Decently strong build hidden under his clothes. A very outside boy. Likes nature and hates being trapped inside. Enjoys getting dirty, and often practices his swordsmanship outside with the guards and soldiers. Very people person, very extroverted. Doesn't expect to have to take the crown being the third prince, he just enjoys his youth to its fullest. Born as the third prince, with two younger sisters, one older sister, and two older brothers. Being the third prince, he didn't get that much attention, which lead to him going out a lot more. He picked up swordsmanship and hopes to one day become a soldier or general, once he's old enough. Slowly began to explore the forest more and more to help refine his swordsmanship skills, which lead to him eventually meeting Silver. Person Relation Notes --- --- --- ▲ Silver Mythrodak Friend/Love Interest First to meet Silver and drag her royal castle and civilized world Swordsmanship Diplomacy Court manners Met Silver first and brought her to the royal capital - [ ]"}, {"t": "Silver Mythrodak", "u": "characters/silver-mythrodak.html", "y": "character", "g": "", "a": "protagonist demi-human hero", "f": "She/Her Demi-Human (Arctic Fox) 19 None 1236 Arcy", "b": "Raised alone in the forest by spirits, she grew up very feral and wild. After the third prince accidentally wanders into her territory and almost dies, she saves him and nurses him back to health in her cabin. He comes back again and again, eventually dragging her back to the castle against her will because of \"danger\" in the forest. Now living in the castle, she messes with the royal family constantly, staying as a guest against her will. Although she eventually learns to love the palace, and decides to stay out of her own free will. White fox ears and two fluffy white fox tails, an unusual genetic deformity in Demi-Humans. Sharp slits and canines, 5/3, with messy, unkept hair. Prefers to typically wear less, skimpier clothing because of growing up in the forest. Brash and bold, she refuses to be held down by people or things. She always pushes forward with determination, but also pretends not to care much for people she's close to. She will push past both royalty and commoners alike, not caring for them or their feelings, but secretly will protect them to her deathbed. Raised alone in the forest by spirits, she grew up very feral and wild. Living in a cabin deep into monster-infected woods. As a child, a yellow haired, bright eyed boy came by to visit her quite often. He gave her, her name, taught her language, writing, swordsmanship and more civilized skills, and became her best friend. One day he disappeared, leaving a note that says he's heading into the mountains. He left her his swords, and a photo of them two as children, which she treasures forever. One of her biggest goals is to find him again one day, not believing that he's dead, despite what everyone tells her. Person Relation Notes --- --- --- ★ Lorian Eros Friend/Love Interest Enhanced senses due to being a Demi-Human fox, able to twist her body in different ways inhumanly due to different bone layouts. Has a double larynx, letting her sing in different tones and double sound, letting her make musical notes and sounds with just her voice. She can move her tails independently as limbs, but they move on their own if she doesn't think about moving them directly. They can be used to hold object, or specifically lets her fight in an unconventional 4 swords style. Dual wielding with both her hands and tails. The target of a Guild hit Arcy is sent on, later in the timeline - [ ] ![](Art/silver-mythrodak/download.jpeg)"}, {"t": "Chapter 1 - On the Farm", "u": "stories/arcy/chapter-1-on-the-farm.html", "y": "chapter", "g": "", "a": "", "f": "Part One 1 1", "b": "Prose goes here. "}, {"t": "Chapter 2 - The Vellhaven Attempt", "u": "stories/arcy/chapter-2-the-vellhaven-attempt.html", "y": "chapter", "g": "", "a": "", "f": "Part One 1 2", "b": "Prose goes here. "}, {"t": "Chapter 3 - Taken In", "u": "stories/arcy/chapter-3-taken-in.html", "y": "chapter", "g": "", "a": "", "f": "Part One 1 3", "b": "Prose goes here. "}, {"t": "Chapter 4 - The Mark", "u": "stories/arcy/chapter-4-the-mark.html", "y": "chapter", "g": "", "a": "", "f": "Part Two 2 4", "b": "Prose goes here. "}, {"t": "Arcy", "u": "stories/arcy.html", "y": "story", "g": "Arcy's backstory", "a": "", "f": "True main timeline 1255 Arcy Ivory Silver Mythrodak Ivory Farm Vellhaven The Basement Amphora", "b": "Arcy's backstory, how she joined the Assassin's Guild, what she wants, and how she got to where she in now Character Role in this story Arc --- --- --- ★ Arcy Ivory Main Character 1 Silver Mythrodak Assassination target 2 Arcy working on Ivory Farm Arcy's father sick Goes to Vellhaven to see royalty visiting from Amphora gets caught up in assassination attempt runs away gets inducted into Assassin's Guild, trained at The Basement time passes attempts assassination on Silver Mythrodak  - [ ]"}, {"t": "Assassin's Guild", "u": "factions/assassins-guild.html", "y": "faction", "g": "\"Client Confidentiality\"", "a": "assassin's guild villain", "f": "Guild The Basement Arcy Ivory", "b": "Wants money more than anything. However, they are fiercely loyal to their members and clients, defending them with their lives. Operates in secret, with no main hub or home base. Will work with little morals and will take hits on anyone except members of their own guild or allies. Anyone can be taken out, given the right price.  Person Rank / Role Loyalty --- --- --- Arcy Ivory Member - [ ] base: points at The Basement, but How They Operate says they keep no main hub. Currently reconciled by treating the Basement as one safehouse among several rather than a headquarters - confirm that reading, or pick a different one and clear the base: field. - [ ] No leader recorded. Does the Guild have one, or is that deliberate? - [ ] Were the assassins at Vellhaven Guild members? Arcy's backstory says she ran with \"the real assassins\" and was recruited afterwards, which does not quite say they were the same organisation."}, {"t": "Royal Guard", "u": "factions/royal-guard.html", "y": "faction", "g": "For the kingdom", "a": "capital territories royalty", "f": "Order Amphora Royal Family Assassin's Guild", "b": "Their goal is to protect the kingdom, civilians, and the royal family. They have a couple thousand members. Spread out across the whole kingdom, they keep watch over the whole kingdom's territories, spread out over many different posts, but centered in the capital. Long time rivalry with Assassin's Guild, always chasing after their tail but never catching them. Classic royal guard. First founded by the first king's bodyguards, then expanded as they hired more and more people. It started in just Amphora- but soon expanded across the cities and territory. Person Rank / Role Loyalty --- --- --- - [ ]"}, {"t": "Amphora", "u": "locations/amphora.html", "y": "location", "g": "The royal capital of the nation, where Eros royal family lives.", "a": "capital territories", "f": "city The Capital Territories Vellhaven Royal Family Royal Guard Silver Mythrodak Lorian Eros", "b": "The seat of the crown and the home of the Eros royal family, at the very center of the kingdom. First made in a sprawling savannah plains, the capital city is often a bustling hub of activity. Always loud and active, only going quieter once curfew hits. More hot temperature typically, and very humid air. Always crowded by people from all races and places, with never a dull moment. Was the first city when The Great Hero took the territory two centuries ago. Since then, the kingdom has expanded greatly, reaching all the way to the sea and mountains, and have certified themselves as one of the more major kingdoms of the world, and the main human kingdom. The capital city itself is a bustling hub of trade, adventure, commerce, diplomacy, and anything else that you can think of. An assassination attempt was made on royals of this city while they were visiting Vellhaven, causing Arcy to join the Assassin's Guild later. Prince Lorian Eros - 3rd Royal Prince of the kingdom Silver Mythrodak - A guest at the royal capital, dragged in by Prince Lorian - Whoever paid for the Vellhaven attempt is more likely to be here than out in the Outskirts. - The Assassin's Guild takes hits on anyone for the right price. The most expensive targets in the kingdom are mostly in this city. - It is the obvious destination for the \"grand adventure\" Arcy has wanted her whole life, and the obvious place for her two lives to collide in public. - [ ] Who sits on the throne, and were they the target at Vellhaven? - [ ] How far is it from Vellhaven - days, or a week? - [ ] Does the Assassin's Guild operate inside the capital, or is it too risky?"}, {"t": "Ivory Farm", "u": "locations/ivory-farm.html", "y": "location", "g": "The ordinary life Arcy is tied to.", "a": "outskirts", "f": "farmstead The Outskirts Vellhaven Arcy Ivory Cherri Ivory", "b": "The Ivory family's farm, out on the thin edge of the kingdom where the worked land gives out. It has fed the family for generations and is currently being run almost single-handedly by Arcy Ivory - her father's illness came on suddenly and her three younger siblings are too young to carry the work. An hour's walk from Vellhaven, which is close enough to sell a cart of produce and be home the same day, and close enough to be somewhere else at night and still make the morning's work. Nothing about the place is remarkable. That is the point of it. It is what Arcy took the Guild's money to keep, and it is the reason she can never leave for long. Everything here is a chore that repeats. The ground is workable but tired, and it takes more out of you each season than it did the last. Sound carries a long way because there's nothing to stop it - you hear a cart on the road well before you see it, which is useful if you have reasons to be seen coming home late.  - Arcy Ivory - eldest; runs the farm since her father fell ill - Cherri Ivory - youngest of the four; out in the fields or the woods whenever she is well enough - Her father - bedridden, name undecided - One more sister and a brother - names undecided - The farm cannot survive Arcy leaving for any length of time. Every adventure has a clock on it. - Guild money is paying for something here. Someone will eventually ask where a farmer's daughter got it. - Her father's illness has no cause yet. It could be nothing, or it could be the first thing that was done to this family on purpose. - [ ] How far is it really from Vellhaven? An hour is what the double life needs - confirm or change it, other distances follow from this one. - [ ] What do they actually farm? Arcy uses a scythe, so grain of some kind. - [ ] Does the farm have a name the family uses, separate from \"the Ivory place\"? - [ ] Are there neighbours, or is it isolated? Changes who could notice her."}, {"t": "The Basement", "u": "locations/the-basement.html", "y": "location", "g": "One of the Guild's safehouses, under something dull.", "a": "assassin's guild hidden", "f": "safehouse Vellhaven The Heartland Vellhaven Assassin's Guild Arcy Ivory", "b": "A cellar beneath an unremarkable building in Vellhaven, used by the Assassin's Guild as a meeting point, a place to hand over payment, and somewhere to wait out a bad night. It is deliberately not a headquarters - one safehouse among an unknown number. Losing it would cost the Guild a room, not an organisation. Where Arcy Ivory was trained, and where she goes when she is not being a farmer. Low ceiling, no windows, one way in that anyone would find and at least one that they wouldn't. It is dry, which is the most anyone will say in its favour. The building above it is chosen for being boring - the point of the place is that nobody has a reason to describe it.  Nobody lives here. People wait here. - Arcy Ivory - trained here; comes at night - If it is compromised, the Guild abandons it without sentiment. Anyone who thought of it as home learns something about the Guild that day. - Payment changes hands here, which means the ledger of who hired whom is here too, at least for a while. - Arcy has to get from the farm to here and back before morning, routinely. The route is a weak point and someone could learn it. - [ ] What is the building above it? A shop, an inn, a chandler's - whatever it is becomes a recurring set. - [ ] Who runs it day to day? The Guild has no leader recorded yet. - [ ] How many other safehouses are there, and does Arcy know of any? - [ ] Is \"The Basement\" what the Guild calls it, or what Arcy calls it?"}, {"t": "Vellhaven", "u": "locations/vellhaven.html", "y": "location", "g": "The market town where Arcy's other life started.", "a": "heartland", "f": "town The Heartland Ivory Farm The Basement Amphora Assassin's Guild Arcy Ivory", "b": "The nearest town to Ivory Farm and the last real stop on the road before Amphora. Big enough to have a market, an inn and a reason for royals to pass through; small enough that a face gets remembered. This is where Arcy Ivory was caught up in the assassination attempt on visiting royals - she was in the wrong part of town on the wrong day, ran with the killers rather than be taken for one, and ended up recruited. The Assassin's Guild keeps The Basement under the town, which means Arcy's two lives are an hour apart. Vellhaven matters because it is the hinge. Everything ordinary is west of it and everything dangerous is east. A working town rather than a pretty one. The market is loud in the morning and dead by mid-afternoon. Because it sits on the road to the capital it gets a steady traffic of people who don't live there, which is exactly why the Guild can operate in it - a stranger is not automatically interesting here. The assassination attempt on the visiting royals happened here. Whether the town recovered quietly or is still under scrutiny is undecided, and it changes a lot. - Arcy Ivory - not a resident; here to sell, and later for other reasons - Someone in Vellhaven saw Arcy run with the assassins and has not said so yet. - The crown may still have people asking questions about the attempt. - A town on the capital road sees everything that passes. Whoever runs the inn knows more than anyone with a title does. - [ ] Who holds authority here - a lord, a council, a crown appointee? - [ ] Did the royal target survive the attempt? This is the biggest unanswered question in the world right now; most politics follows from the answer. - [ ] Was the attempt Guild work, or a rival's? Arcy ran with \"the real assassins\" - her file doesn't say they were Guild."}];
